      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "AFRICAN DIAMOND (4) consistent mare resuming with excellent fresh credentials. Lone victory came at this track and trip and kicks off in a winnable race with the one trial over 1000m. Can stalk the speed and prove hard to stop. GELSEY (3) struck some trouble at the start and gave away too much start on the turn with a battling seventh over 1250m at Gunnedah. Comes back a few grades and should be ready to peak. VLTAVA (1) resumes on his home track after making solid progress last time in. Claim helps from the right gate and will be savaging the line. ENSIGN PARKER (2) strips fitter and will relish the class drop after he faded to finish eighth over 1350m at Beaumont (Newcastle). Should stalk the pace and figure prominently.",
